<body>
    <h1>Troubleshooting: PixStor Filesystem Not Mounted on AI+ Ubuntu Serve=
r</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h2 id=3D"Troubleshooting:PixStorFilesystemNotMountedonAI+UbuntuSer=
ver-Overview">Overview</h2>
<p>This guide explains how to diagnose and fix the issue where the PixStor/=
GPFS filesystem (<code>mmfs1</code>) appears as an empty directory and does=
 not show up in <code>df -h</code>.</p>
<p>Symptoms include:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><code>/mmfs1</code> can be listed, but only shows empty subdirectories (=
no data).</p></li>
<li>
<p><code>df -h</code> does not display <code>mmfs1</code> as a mounted file=
system.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Running GPFS commands (<code>mmgetstate</code>, <code>mmmount</code>, <c=
ode>mmlsmount</code>) results in <code>command not found</code>.</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"Troubleshooting:PixStorFilesystemNotMountedonAI+UbuntuServer-Root=
Cause">Root Cause</h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The GPFS binaries were not in the system <code>PATH</code>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>SSH trust between the AI+ server and PixStor cluster nodes was not estab=
lished, causing GPFS commands to hang or fail.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The filesystem was not mounted locally on the AI+ server.</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"Troubleshooting:PixStorFilesystemNotMountedonAI+UbuntuServer-Solu=
tion">Solution</h2>
<h3 id=3D"Troubleshooting:PixStorFilesystemNotMountedonAI+UbuntuServer-Step=
1:ConfirmGPFSPackagesareInstalled">Step 1: Confirm GPFS Packages are Instal=
led</h3>
<p>Run:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">dpkg -l=
 | grep gpfs
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>You should see packages like <code>gpfs.base</code>, <code>gpfs.license.=
std</code>, etc.<br>
If they are missing, the PixStor client is not installed.</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"Troubleshooting:PixStorFilesystemNotMountedonAI+UbuntuServer-Step=
2:VerifyGPFSBinariesLocation">Step 2: Verify GPFS Binaries Location</h3>
<p>Check if binaries exist:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">ls /usr=
/lpp/mmfs/bin
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>If present, prepend this directory to your PATH:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">export =
PATH=3D$PATH:/usr/lpp/mmfs/bin
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>(Optional: make permanent by adding to <code>/etc/profile.d/gpfs.sh</cod=
e>.)</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"Troubleshooting:PixStorFilesystemNotMountedonAI+UbuntuServer-Step=
3:FixHostnameResolution">Step 3: Fix Hostname Resolution</h3>
<p>Ensure <code>/etc/hosts</code> maps the AI+ server correctly:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sudoedi=
t /etc/hosts
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Add or fix:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">192.168=
.18.244  per-ai
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Remove any line mapping <code>per-ai</code> to <code>127.0.1.1</code>.</=
p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"Troubleshooting:PixStorFilesystemNotMountedonAI+UbuntuServer-Step=
4:ResetSSHKnownHosts">Step 4: Reset SSH Known Hosts</h3>
<p>Clear old host key entries and re-seed them:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">for h i=
n per-ai alt-mn-001.pixstor alt-sn-001.pixstor alt-gw-001.pixstor alt-ng-00=
1.pixstor alt-nvme-001.pixstor \
         127.0.1.1 10.100.0.1 10.100.0.2 10.100.0.3 10.100.0.4 10.100.0.5 ;=
 do
  ssh-keygen -R "$h" &gt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1 || true
done

ssh-keyscan -H per-ai alt-mn-001.pixstor alt-sn-001.pixstor alt-gw-001.pixs=
tor alt-ng-001.pixstor alt-nvme-001.pixstor \
             10.100.0.1 10.100.0.2 10.100.0.3 10.100.0.4 10.100.0.5 &gt;&gt=
; ~/.ssh/known_hosts
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"Troubleshooting:PixStorFilesystemNotMountedonAI+UbuntuServer-Step=
5:VerifySSHAccesstoClusterNodes">Step 5: Verify SSH Access to Cluster Nodes=
</h3>
<p>Log in once to each PixStor node as <code>root</code> (password from env=
ironment documentation, typically <code>edison02</code>):</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">ssh roo=
t@alt-mn-001.pixstor
ssh root@alt-sn-001.pixstor
ssh root@alt-gw-001.pixstor
ssh root@alt-ng-001.pixstor
ssh root@alt-nvme-001.pixstor
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Accept fingerprints and confirm you can log in. This step ensures GPFS c=
an communicate without blocking.</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"Troubleshooting:PixStorFilesystemNotMountedonAI+UbuntuServer-Step=
6:StartGPFSLocally">Step 6: Start GPFS Locally</h3>
<p>On the AI+ node (<code>per-ai</code>):</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sudo mm=
startup
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Check state:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sudo mm=
getstate -N per-ai
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>You should see:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Node nu=
mber  Node name  GPFS state
-------------------------------------
7            per-ai     active
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"Troubleshooting:PixStorFilesystemNotMountedonAI+UbuntuServer-Step=
7:MounttheFilesystem">Step 7: Mount the Filesystem</h3>
<p>Mount <code>mmfs1</code> on the AI+ server only:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sudo mm=
mount mmfs1 -N per-ai
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Verify:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sudo mm=
lsmount mmfs1
df -h | grep mmfs
ls -lah /mmfs1/data/space01
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Expected output:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><code>mmfs1</code> shows in <code>df -h</code></p></li>
<li>
<p><code>/mmfs1/data/space01</code> contains media data</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"Troubleshooting:PixStorFilesystemNotMountedonAI+UbuntuServer-Fina=
lVerification">Final Verification</h2>
<p>If successful:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">df -h |=
 grep mmfs
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Shows something like:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">mmfs1  =
         224T   26T  199T  12% /mmfs1
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>And:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">ls /mmf=
s1/data/space01
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Shows customer/media content.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"Troubleshooting:PixStorFilesystemNotMountedonAI+UbuntuServer-Note=
s">Notes</h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Always use <code>-N per-ai</code> when mounting or starting locally to a=
void SSH fan-out to all nodes.</p></li>
<li>
<p>If SSH trust is broken again, repeat <strong>Step 4 + Step 5</strong>.</=
p></li>
<li>
<p>For repeated use, configure sudoers to allow limited GPFS commands witho=
ut full root login.</p></li>
</ul>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
